event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":87,"item_id":"rs_06c431951bef740e016ac9dffee3fc8193b7ccb8b8a5b204e7","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Implementing SSR forms**\n\nI'm thinking about how to create simple server-side rendered (SSR) forms with POST redirects while ensuring accessibility. I want to utilize the browser's native form validation instead of custom errors and avoid using required fields. No JSON is necessary here, but I need to ensure the server escapes any inputs. Also, I should build tests to spawn temporary databases for requests and maintain persistence for health checks on rendered pages and forms routes."}

